config ECC_CRC32
	bool "CRC-32 based ECC library"
	select CRC
	help
	  Enables the CRC-32 based error detection and correction library.
	  Provides 1-bit correction and optional 2-bit correction for data
	  buffers using CRC-32 (polynomial 0x04C11DB7, reflected).

	  For 2-bit correction the codeword (data + 4-byte CRC) must not
	  exceed 371 bytes.

if ECC_CRC32

config ECC_CRC32_2BIT_CORRECTION
	bool "Enable 2-bit error correction"
	default n
	help
	  Enables O(n²) brute-force 2-bit error correction in addition to
	  1-bit correction.

	  WARNING: on a Cortex-M33 at 160 MHz this takes ~250 ms per
	  uncorrectable page (codeword_bits = 2048, inner loop = 4M
	  iterations).  Any bulk read that hits multiple uncorrectable pages
	  will stall for minutes and may starve cooperative threads or
	  trigger a watchdog reset.

	  Leave disabled unless the application explicitly needs 2-bit
	  correction and can tolerate the latency.  With this disabled,
	  pages with 2-bit (or higher) errors are still correctly detected
	  and reported as UNCORRECTABLE; only correction is skipped.

endif # ECC_CRC32
